Foreign Currency Exposure
The Company is exposed to certain price risks such as foreign exchange rate as well as interest rate risks, changes in commodity prices and in the price of its own stocks.Adverse movements of these prices may jeopardise the Company’s proﬁ tability if not hedged.Airbus intends to generate proﬁ ts only from its operations and not through speculation on the development of such prices.The Company uses hedging strategies to manage and minimise the impact of such price ﬂ uctuations on its proﬁ ts, including foreign currency derivative contracts, interest rate and equity swaps and other non-derivative ﬁ nancial assets or liabilities denominated in a foreign currency.

